    "evidence": "Clover's developer docs index and Platform API reference document employee create, update and delete endpoints but no SCIM or SSO; the pricing page and help centre are client-rendered and could not be read, so SCIM status stays unknown.",
    "notes": "New row. Clover (Fiserv) POS. www.clover.com/pricing and the help centre are JavaScript single-page apps that returned only a title to curl and WebFetch, and the headless renderer failed (ERR_TOO_MANY_RETRIES), so no prices or plan feature lists were captured and pricing_page_url points at the developer docs plan page; plan names come from the developer docs (US/Canada: Payments/Payments Plus, Essentials/Register Lite, Register, Counter Service Restaurant, Table Service Restaurant). The developer docs index (docs.clover.com/dev/llms.txt) has no SCIM, SAML or SSO page. The Platform REST API (OAuth bearer tokens) exposes employees and roles CRUD per merchant, and webhooks fire on employee create/update/delete. No Okta or Entra catalogue app found. Kept unknown rather than none because the pricing page and help centre were not reachable (rule 5).",
